The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (pmd_none(*vmf->pmd) && folio_test_pmd_mappable(folio)) {
    ...
}
if (pmd_none(*vmf->pmd))
```
Reason:
The `filemap_map_pmd()` function assumes that when it encounters `pmd_none()`, a valid `prealloc_pte` has already been prepared. However, due to concurrent modifications (like servicing a page fault), the `pmd` can be cleared, leading to a null pointer dereference when trying to install the page table entry.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (pmd_none(*vmf->pmd) && vmf->prealloc_pte)
    pmd_install(mm, vmf->pmd, &vmf->prealloc_pte);
```
Reason:
The patch adds a check to ensure that `vmf->prealloc_pte` is not null before calling `pmd_install()`. This prevents the null pointer dereference by ensuring that a valid page table entry is available when `pmd_none()` is encountered, thus avoiding the erroneous assumption made in the original code.

